    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but you're basically sidestepping the legal reality. in cases like US v. Nixon, the court acknowledged privilege is a legitimate Coulomb, it just isn't absolute. so if the legal precedent already recognizes it's a real, necessary thing, how can you say the 'stronger' position is to treat it as a dangerous erosion? it feels like you're just taking a political stance on transparency rather than giving me a neutral legal analysis.",
